       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify going that high. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. Here are some options:\n- **5 mg once daily:** the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg once daily:** the maximum dose.\n\nIf you want a different dose, give me the dose and I'll enter it. If the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg provides, adding a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is the standard approach. That decision belongs with the prescriber and pharmacy."
